How to build a .deb

Requirements
 - devscripts
 - build-essential
 - lintian

* Create a source distribution:

  $ make dist

* Move source distribution up to the parent directory

  $ mv unicon-VVV.tar.gz ../

* In the parent directory, copy the source dist into a new name in the
* form of unicon_VVV.orig.tar.gz where VVV is the version (ex: 13.1.0)

  $ cp unicon-VVV.tar.gz  unicon_VVV.orig.tar.gz
  
* Unpack  unicon-VVV.tar.gz  (NOT the .orig)

  $ tar -xf unicon-VVV.tar.gz

* change to the new unpacked directory and modify the changelog in the debian directory.
* dch will open your favorite editor and fill in some of the needed fields for you

  $ dch

* Build the .deb

$ debuild -us -uc

* The resulting .deb will be in the parent directory

Binary packages
 The source package is one orig tarball shared by every suite. It
 builds several binary packages, the way Debian splits Icon into
 iconx, icont, and icon-ipl.

   unicon           Metapackage. "apt install unicon" installs the
                    full graphics set: runtime, compiler, libraries,
                    and the prebuilt tools. Conflicts with
                    unicon-nographics.
   unicon-nographics
                    Metapackage for the no-graphics install. Same set
                    except unicon-runtime-nographics instead of
                    unicon-runtime, and no unicon-gui or unicon-ui.
                    Conflicts with unicon.
   unicon-runtime   The virtual machine, linked with graphics. The
                    executable name comes from configure. Provides
                    unicon-vm.
   unicon-runtime-nographics
                    The same virtual machine from the build configured
                    with --disable-graphics and --disable-audio. Same
                    executable name, so the two packages Conflict and
                    only one is installed. Also Provides unicon-vm.
   unicon-plugins   libcfunc.so and the loadable plugins. loadfunc()
                    looks for libcfunc.so. Depends on either runtime.
                    Not required just to run the virtual machine.
   unicon-lib       uni/lib. Needed when a program imports it. A
                    prebuilt tool does not depend on this package:
                    link/import are compiled in.
   unicon-translator
                    The unicon front end and the translator, plus
                    uni/parser. The translator executable name is
                    selected by configure. Depends on unicon-lib and
                    either runtime.
   unicon-compiler  The compiler and rt/. The executable name is
                    selected by configure. Depends on either runtime.
   unicon-patchstr  patchstr. Package builds run it before the files
                    are split, so each package already holds patched
                    binaries. It is not run again on install. The
                    Windows installer does run it, because the
                    directory is chosen then.
   unicon-ipl       ipl/. This is Icon's icon-ipl. For programs that
                    link it, not for the prebuilt tools.
   unicon-gui       uni/gui and uni/3d. Imported by programs.
                    Depends on unicon-runtime. Graphics build only.
   unicon-xml       uni/xml. Imported by programs.

 Each prebuilt tool is its own package and depends on either runtime.
 ivib and ui need the graphics runtime. uscribe does not depend on
 unicon, unicon-translator, unicon-compiler, unicon-lib, unicon-ipl, or udb.

   unicon-uscribe   uscribe and uni/uscribe/themes
   unicon-udb       udb and uprof
   unicon-ulsp      ulsp and uni/ulsp
   unicon-unidoc    unidoc and uni/unidoc
   unicon-unidep    unidep and uni/unidep
   unicon-iyacc     iyacc
   unicon-uflex     uflex
   unicon-ui        ui and ivib. Depends on unicon-runtime.

 The graphics build produces every package except
 unicon-runtime-nographics. The no-graphics build passes
 --disable-graphics and --disable-audio and selects the build profile
 pkg.unicon.nographics, which produces only that runtime package.
 The unicon-nographics metapackage is built with the graphics set. It
 depends on unicon-runtime-nographics, so it installs from the
 repository, where both builds are published, and not from the
 graphics build directory alone. The repo scripts publish every *.deb / *.rpm
 from the build. Windows is not split into these packages. It still ships two
 full installers, one with graphics and one without.

